<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · China, Tibet and Mongolia</p><h1 class="st-title">First East Turkestan Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1933 CE – 1934 CE · capital Kashgar</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A short-lived Islamic republic proclaimed at Kashgar in 1933 during the rebellions in Xinjiang, the first attempt at an independent Uyghur state.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The abolition of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kumul-khanate">Kumul Khanate</a> in 1930 provoked revolts across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xinjiang">Xinjiang</a> against Governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jin-shuren">Jin Shuren</a>. In the south, rebels from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-khotan">Khotan</a> led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-amin-bughra">Muhammad Amin Bughra</a> and the cleric <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sabit-damulla">Sabit Damulla</a> took <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-shule">Kashgar</a>, and on 12 November 1933 proclaimed the Turkish Islamic Republic of East Turkestan.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The republic was based on Islamic law and Turkic nationalism, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sabit-damulla">Sabit Damulla</a> as prime minister and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hami">Kumul</a> rebel leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khoja-niyaz">Khoja Niyaz</a> named president, though he never ruled from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-shule">Kashgar</a>. It had a constitution, flag and coins but little control beyond the southern oases, and it failed to win recognition from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> or <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/islamic-emirate-of-afghanistan-2021-present">Afghanistan</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In early 1934 Hui Muslim troops of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ma-zhongying">Ma Zhongying</a>, retreating from the north, took <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-shule">Kashgar</a> and crushed the republic. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khoja-niyaz">Khoja Niyaz</a> came to terms with the new governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sheng-shicai">Sheng Shicai</a> and handed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sabit-damulla">Sabit Damulla</a> over. The idea revived in the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/second-east-turkestan-republic">Second East Turkestan Republic</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/first-east-turkestan-republic.jpg" alt="First East Turkestan Republic" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Tarkan · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kokbayraq_flag.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1933 CE – 1934 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>theocratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kashgar</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Khoja Niyaz, Sabit Damulla</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Uyghur</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/china">China</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Turkish Islamic Republic of East Turkestan</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1934&amp;focus=first-east-turkestan-republic" aria-label="First East Turkestan Republic on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6557 764 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where First East Turkestan Republic lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6877 1020L8221 1549"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M8221 1549h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6877 1020h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6877 1020h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Kashgar. <a href="/atlas?year=1934&amp;focus=first-east-turkestan-republic">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
